    "design": "This was a fluid-volume trial: an international, randomized trial comparing restricted intravenous fluid with standard intravenous fluid therapy. The primary outcome was death from any cause within 90 days after randomization.",
    "population": "Patients with septic shock in the ICU who had received at least 1 liter of intravenous fluid, enrolled if the onset of shock was within 12 hours before screening. 1554 patients were enrolled; 770 were assigned to the restrictive-fluid group and 784 to the standard-fluid group. Primary outcome data were available for 1545 patients (99.4%).",
