    "population": "Patients with acute respiratory failure or shock and hypoactive or hyperactive delirium. Written informed consent was obtained from 1183 patients or their authorized representatives. Delirium developed in 566 patients (48%), of whom 89% had hypoactive delirium and 11% had hyperactive delirium. Of these, 184 were assigned to placebo, 192 to haloperidol, and 190 to ziprasidone. The median duration of exposure to a trial drug or placebo was 4 days (interquartile range, 3 to 7).",
