    "population": "Patients aged 18 years or older requiring invasive mechanical ventilation within 24 hours of ICU admission were eligible. Patients with an ICU admission diagnosis of upper gastrointestinal bleeding were excluded. Among 26 982 patients who were randomized, 154 opted out, and 26 828 were analyzed, of whom 13 436 were assigned to proton pump inhibitors as the default and 13 392 were assigned to histamine-2 receptor blockers. There were 26 771 patients (99.2%) included in the mortality analysis.",
